  {
   "id": "fact-005",
   "kind": "text",
   "role": "assistant",
   "conversation": "conv-1",
   "evidence": "wire",
   "value": {
    "text": "For your two-day Barcelona trip, pack light, layerable clothing suited to mild temperatures of 21-22°C, including two or three t-shirts or breathable tops, a light sweater or cardigan for cooler evenings, and a pair of comfortable pants or jeans plus one pair of shorts or a skirt for the sunny second day. Since Day 1 brings rain, bring a compact, packable rain jacket or small umbrella and water-resistant shoes or sneakers that can handle wet cobblestones, along with a spare pair of socks. For Day 2's sunshine, add sunglasses, sunscreen, and a hat or cap, and consider a reusable water bottle for walking around the city. Round out your bag with essentials like underwear, sleepwear, a phone charger, toiletries, your passport or ID, a small daypack or crossbody bag (preferably with zippers, as Barcelona's busy areas attract pickpockets), and a plastic bag to separate any damp items."
   },
   "require": {
